  "title": "Founding of OPEC",
  "summary": "At a conference in Baghdad held 10–14 September 1960, Iran, Iraq, Kuwait, Saudi Arabia and Venezuela set up the Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries as a permanent body. Its stated purpose was to unify member oil policies and safeguard members' interests; a U.S. memo links its creation to oil companies' cuts in posted prices in August 1960.",
